        },
        reflection: "Today's parable of the sower reminds us that God's word is like seed scattered generously. The question is not whether God's word is powerful - it always is. The question is what kind of soil our hearts provide. Are we the path where the word bounces off? The rocky ground where it starts but doesn't take root? The thorny ground where worldly concerns choke it out? Or are we the good soil where God's word can grow and bear fruit? Let us examine our hearts today and ask God to make us good soil for His word."
